{"name":"Sand Dance","hex":"#e0c8b9","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sand","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Rock that is ground more finely than gravel, but is not as fine as silt (more formally, see grain sizes chart), forming beaches and deserts and also used in construction.\n\n A specific grade, type, or composition of sand.\n\n A beach or other mass of sand.","A specific grade, type, or composition of sand."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a light beige colour, like that of typical sand."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sand"},{"term":"dance","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sequence of rhythmic steps or movements usually performed to music, for pleasure or as a form of social interaction.","A social gathering where dancing is the main activity."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move with rhythmic steps or movements, especially in time to music.","To leap or move lightly and rapidly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dance"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wilson, Keppel and Betty","blocks":[{"text":"Wilson, Keppel and Betty formed a popular British music hall and vaudeville act, active primarily from 1928 to the early 60s. They capitalised on the fashion for Ancient Egyptian imagery following the discovery of the tomb of Tutankhamun. The \"sand dance\" that formed the highlight of their act was a parody of postures from Egyptian tomb paintings, combined with references to Arab costume. The lithe and extremely lanky Wilson and Keppel, who wore long moustaches and make-up to emphasise the sharp angularity of their features and make them appear almost identical, demonstrated their impressive suppleness in adopting wild gestures and dancing in identical \"stereo\" movements, while Betty joined their antics. The act included a soft-shoe routine performed on a layer of sand spread on the stage to create a rhythmic scratching with their shuffling feet and was usually performed to the familiar Egyptian Ballet (1875), by Alexandre Luigini."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e7/1939_Wilson%2C_Keppel_and_Betty.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wilson%2C_Keppel_and_Betty","wikidata":"Q8022930"},{"title":"Sand","blocks":[{"text":"Sand is a granular material composed of finely divided mineral particles. Sand has various compositions but is usually defined by its grain size. Sand grains are smaller than gravel and coarser than silt. Sand can also refer to a textural class of soil or soil type; i.e., a soil containing more than 85 percent sand-sized particles by mass."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Libya_4608_Idehan_Ubari_Dunes_Luca_Galuzzi_2007.jpg/330px-Libya_4608_Idehan_Ubari_Dunes_Luca_Galuzzi_2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sand","wikidata":"Q34679"},{"title":"Dance","blocks":[{"text":"Dance is an art form, consisting of sequences of body movements with aesthetic and often symbolic value, either improvised or purposefully selected. Dance can be categorized and described by its choreography, by its repertoire of movements or by its historical period or place of origin. Dance is typically performed with musical accompaniment, and sometimes with the dancer simultaneously using a musical instrument themselves."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Two_dancers.jpg/330px-Two_dancers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dance","wikidata":"Q11639"},{"title":"Desert sand (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Desert sand is a very light and very weakly saturated reddish yellow color which corresponds specifically to the coloration of sand. It may also be regarded as a deep tone of beige."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Sossusvlei_Dune_Namib_Desert_Namibia_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG/330px-Sossusvlei_Dune_Namib_Desert_Namibia_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desert_sand_(color)","wikidata":"Q9303163"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/ca/Wilsonkeppelandbetty1933.jpg/330px-Wilsonkeppelandbetty1933.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/ca/Wilsonkeppelandbetty1933.jpg/330px-Wilsonkeppelandbetty1933.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wilson, Keppel and Betty photographed in 1928","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWilsonkeppelandbetty1933.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Female_war_correspondents_World_War_II.jpg/500px-Female_war_correspondents_World_War_II.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Female_war_correspondents_World_War_II.jpg/1280px-Female_war_correspondents_World_War_II.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Female_war_correspondents_World_War_II.jpg/500px-Female_war_correspondents_World_War_II.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Betty Knox (third from right) in 1944 as a war correspondent for the London Evening Standard","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFemale_war_correspondents_World_War_II.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d9/Wilson_Keppel_Sand_Dance.jpg/250px-Wilson_Keppel_Sand_Dance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d9/Wilson_Keppel_Sand_Dance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d9/Wilson_Keppel_Sand_Dance.jpg/250px-Wilson_Keppel_Sand_Dance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wilson and Keppel perform their Sand Dance routine in 1934.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWilson_Keppel_Sand_Dance.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/00065_sand_collage.jpg/500px-00065_sand_collage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/00065_sand_collage.jpg/1280px-00065_sand_collage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/00065_sand_collage.jpg/500px-00065_sand_collage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Depiction of sands: glass, dune, quartz, volcanic, biogenic coral, pink coral,volcanic, garnet, olivine.Samples are from the Gobi Desert, Estonia, Hawaii and the mainland United States. (1×1 cm each)[1]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A00065_sand_collage.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/HeavyMineralsBeachSand.jpg/500px-HeavyMineralsBeachSand.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/HeavyMineralsBeachSand.jpg/1280px-HeavyMineralsBeachSand.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/HeavyMineralsBeachSand.jpg/500px-HeavyMineralsBeachSand.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Heavy minerals (dark) in a quartz beach sand (Chennai, India)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHeavyMineralsBeachSand.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://